infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Division of labor: compiler vs manual memo
  desc The compiler does not retire manual memo — it narrows it to jobs it structurally cannot reach
  compares
    - label React Compiler
      children
        - label Per-expression caching
          desc Values, JSX subtrees, function identities
        - label Finer-grained than useMemo
          desc Skips unchanged subtrees component-wide
        - label Only where Rules of React hold
          desc Pure, no mutation, unconditional hooks
        - label Only code in your pipeline
          desc Compiles your app, never node_modules
    - label Manual memo
      children
        - label Published library components
          desc Consumers never compile your node_modules
        - label Non-component caches & selectors
          desc Module caches, reselect, pure fns
        - label Bridges over known bailouts
          desc Until the rule violation is fixed
        - label Referential identity for effects
          desc Deps arrays, context values: correctness
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
